  "aliases": [],
  "title": "A Contributor+ stored cross-site scripting (XSS) issue in Customizer selective refresh",
  "summary": "A user with the Contributor role or above can store markup in post content that Customizer selective refresh treats as HTML, which runs a script in an Administrator's Customizer preview.\r\n\r\nWordPress 7.1.4 has been released containing a fix for the vulnerability, and as a courtesy to users on older branches the fix has been backported to all branches back to 5.0.\r\n\r\nDiscovered and responsibly disclosed by [Rafie Muhammad](https://www.linkedin.com/in/rafiemuhammad/) (Awesome Motive, Inc.)",
